{%- comment -%}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  OTODOR Snippet: Specification Seed lookup
  Part of the Specification Rendering Engine — see OTODOR-SPEC-ENGINE.md.
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Purpose:   Read ONE value out of a column's seed block — a plain
             `spec_id = value` list a merchant can paste into the theme
             editor before the product's specs.* metafields exist.

  The seed is the LOWEST-priority source. Consumers pass the result as
  `spec_default` to otodor-spec-value, so a real metafield always wins and
  the seed silently retires as admin data lands. It is a bridge, not a
  data model — never read it in place of a metafield.

  Params:
    seed  multiline text: one `spec_id = value` per line.
          Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored.
    id    registry spec id to look up (e.g. `door_thickness`).

  Echoes the matching value, or nothing.

  Example seed:
    # SENTRY
    dimensions = 41.5 × 7 cm
    face_recognition = Yes (up to 20)
    door_thickness = 45–100 mm
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  if seed != blank and id != blank
    assign want = id | strip | downcase
    assign lines = seed | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
    for ln in lines
      assign l = ln | strip
      if l == blank
        continue
      endif
      assign first_char = l | slice: 0
      if first_char == '#'
        continue
      endif
      assign parts = l | split: '='
      if parts.size < 2
        continue
      endif
      assign k = parts[0] | strip | downcase
      if k == want
        assign v = l | remove_first: parts[0] | remove_first: '=' | strip
        echo v
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
